{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TLC3Sv4vRWRZpERHog9g19","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tsource_url: \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/opencontainers/image-spec/main/layer.md\"\n3\tfetched_at: \"2026-08-24T01:05:00-0400\"\n4\tauthority: \"Open Container Initiative (Linux Foundation) — OCI Image Format Specification, Image Layer Filesystem Changeset\"\n5\tobjectives_covered: [\"D1.4\"]\n6\tconcepts_covered: [\"image-layers\", \"oci-image-spec\"]\n7\t---\n8\t# OCI Image Layer Filesystem Changeset\n9\t\n10\t> CLOSES THE OPEN HALF OF G29 (layer mechanics). Chapter 2 §2 and ch02-fig02.\n11\t\n12\t## What a layer is\n13\t\n14\t\"This document describes how to serialize a filesystem and filesystem changes like\n15\tremoved files into a blob called a layer. One or more layers are applied on top of\n16\teach other to create a complete filesystem.\"\n17\t\n18\t## Change types\n19\t\n20\t\"Types of changes that can occur in a changeset are: Additions, Modifications,\n21\tRemovals. Additions and Modifications are represented the same in the changeset tar\n22\tarchive.\"\n23\t\n24\t## Tar archives and media types\n25\t\n26\t\"Layer Changesets for the media type `application/vnd.oci.image.layer.v1.tar` MUST be\n27\tpackaged in tar archive.\"\n28\t\n29\t\"Layer Changesets for the media type `application/vnd.oci.image.layer.v1.tar` MUST NOT\n30\tinclude duplicate entries for file paths in the resulting tar archive.\"\n31\t\n32\t\"The media type `application/vnd.oci.image.layer.v1.tar+gzip` represents an\n33\t`application/vnd.oci.image.layer.v1.tar` payload which has been compressed with gzip.\"\n34\t\n35\t## Applying changesets\n36\t\n37\t\"Layer Changesets of media type `application/vnd.oci.image.layer.v1.tar` are applied,\n38\trather than simply extracted as tar archives. Applying a layer changeset requires\n39\tspecial consideration for the whiteout files.\"\n40\t\n41\t## Whiteout files — DEPTH, likely out of scope\n42\t\n43\t\"A whiteout file is an empty file with a special filename that signifies a path should\n44\tbe deleted. A whiteout filename consists of the prefix `.wh.` plus the basename of the\n45\tpath to be deleted.\"\n46\t\n47\tBelow KCNA's waterline. Suitable for a 🔭 Closer Look at most; cut without regret.\n48\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"714f732e-6165-42bf-8392-8c603f3d60fe","uuid":"502adc02-6de7-450c-80d0-8a0d1b4b0562","timestamp":"2026-08-24T19:11:49.003Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\sources\\oci-image-spec-layers-2026-08-24.md","content":"---\nsource_url: \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/opencontainers/image-spec/main/layer.md\"\nfetched_at: \"2026-08-24T01:05:00-0400\"\nauthority: \"Open Container Initiative (Linux Foundation) — OCI Image Format Specification, Image Layer Filesystem Changeset\"\nobjectives_covered: [\"D1.4\"]\nconcepts_covered: [\"image-layers\", \"oci-image-spec\"]\n---\n# OCI Image Layer Filesystem Changeset\n\n> CLOSES THE OPEN HALF OF G29 (layer mechanics). Chapter 2 §2 and ch02-fig02.\n\n## What a layer is\n\n\"This document describes how to serialize a filesystem and filesystem changes like\nremoved files into a blob called a layer. One or more layers are applied on top of\neach other to create a complete filesystem.\"\n\n## Change types\n\n\"Types of changes that can occur in a changeset are: Additions, Modifications,\nRemovals. Additions and Modifications are represented the same in the changeset tar\narchive.\"\n\n## Tar archives and media types\n\n\"Layer Changesets for the media type `application/vnd.oci.image.layer.v1.tar` MUST be\npackaged in tar archive.\"\n\n\"Layer Changesets for the media type `application/vnd.oci.image.layer.v1.tar` MUST NOT\ninclude duplicate entries for file paths in the resulting tar archive.\"\n\n\"The media type `application/vnd.oci.image.layer.v1.tar+gzip` represents an\n`application/vnd.oci.image.layer.v1.tar` payload which has been compressed with gzip.\"\n\n## Applying changesets\n\n\"Layer Changesets of media type `application/vnd.oci.image.layer.v1.tar` are applied,\nrather than simply extracted as tar archives. Applying a layer changeset requires\nspecial consideration for the whiteout files.\"\n\n## Whiteout files — DEPTH, likely out of scope\n\n\"A whiteout file is an empty file with a special filename that signifies a path should\nbe deleted. A whiteout filename consists of the prefix `.wh.` plus the basename of the\npath to be deleted.\"\n\nBelow KCNA's waterline. Suitable for a 🔭 Closer Look at most; cut without regret.\n","numLines":48,"startLine":1,"totalLines":48}}}
