{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QQrkFTruAfMNZbghfLyxnB","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tsource_url: \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/opencontainers/distribution-spec/main/spec.md\"\n3\tfetched_at: \"2026-08-24T01:05:00-0400\"\n4\tauthority: \"Open Container Initiative (Linux Foundation) — OCI Distribution Specification\"\n5\tobjectives_covered: [\"D1.4\"]\n6\tconcepts_covered: [\"oci-distribution-spec\", \"registry\", \"image-digest\"]\n7\t---\n8\t# OCI Distribution Specification\n9\t\n10\t## What it defines\n11\t\n12\t\"The Open Container Initiative Distribution Specification (a.k.a. \\\"OCI Distribution\n13\tSpec\\\") defines an API protocol to facilitate and standardize the distribution of\n14\tcontent.\"\n15\t\n16\t## Definitions\n17\t\n18\t- Registry: \"a service that handles the required APIs defined in this specification\"\n19\t- Repository: \"a scope for API calls on a registry for a collection of content\n20\t  (including manifests, blobs, and tags).\"\n21\t- Blob: \"the binary form of content that is stored by a registry, addressable by a\n22\t  digest\"\n23\t- Manifest: \"a JSON document uploaded via the manifests endpoint. A manifest may\n24\t  reference other manifests and blobs in a repository via descriptors.\"\n25\t- Digest: \"a unique identifier created from a cryptographic hash of a Blob's content.\"\n26\t\n27\t## Workflows\n28\t\n29\t\"Push: the act of uploading blobs and manifests to a registry\"\n30\t\"Pull: the act of downloading blobs and manifests from a registry\"\n31\t\n32\t## Note for §5\n33\t\n34\tThe Digest definition is Fixed Point #1's identity half stated by the standards body.\n35\tThe Registry definition upgrades §5's back-bearing to §3 from \"standardizes the API\"\n36\tto a spec-level definition of what a registry IS. Version date (v1.0, May 2020) lives\n37\tin oci-overview-2026-08-23.md.\n38\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"714f732e-6165-42bf-8392-8c603f3d60fe","uuid":"b3bb1511-4365-4f10-941b-94cf134c8a36","timestamp":"2026-08-24T19:11:55.346Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\sources\\oci-distribution-spec-2026-08-24.md","content":"---\nsource_url: \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/opencontainers/distribution-spec/main/spec.md\"\nfetched_at: \"2026-08-24T01:05:00-0400\"\nauthority: \"Open Container Initiative (Linux Foundation) — OCI Distribution Specification\"\nobjectives_covered: [\"D1.4\"]\nconcepts_covered: [\"oci-distribution-spec\", \"registry\", \"image-digest\"]\n---\n# OCI Distribution Specification\n\n## What it defines\n\n\"The Open Container Initiative Distribution Specification (a.k.a. \\\"OCI Distribution\nSpec\\\") defines an API protocol to facilitate and standardize the distribution of\ncontent.\"\n\n## Definitions\n\n- Registry: \"a service that handles the required APIs defined in this specification\"\n- Repository: \"a scope for API calls on a registry for a collection of content\n  (including manifests, blobs, and tags).\"\n- Blob: \"the binary form of content that is stored by a registry, addressable by a\n  digest\"\n- Manifest: \"a JSON document uploaded via the manifests endpoint. A manifest may\n  reference other manifests and blobs in a repository via descriptors.\"\n- Digest: \"a unique identifier created from a cryptographic hash of a Blob's content.\"\n\n## Workflows\n\n\"Push: the act of uploading blobs and manifests to a registry\"\n\"Pull: the act of downloading blobs and manifests from a registry\"\n\n## Note for §5\n\nThe Digest definition is Fixed Point #1's identity half stated by the standards body.\nThe Registry definition upgrades §5's back-bearing to §3 from \"standardizes the API\"\nto a spec-level definition of what a registry IS. Version date (v1.0, May 2020) lives\nin oci-overview-2026-08-23.md.\n","numLines":38,"startLine":1,"totalLines":38}}}
