{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HWcZT4iHKLVs5f3EhiguMW","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tsource_url: \"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/architecture/cri/\"\n3\tfetched_at: \"2026-08-24T01:05:00-0400\"\n4\tauthority: \"Kubernetes project (kubernetes.io/docs)\"\n5\tobjectives_covered: [\"D1.4\"]\n6\tconcepts_covered: [\"cri\", \"container-runtime\", \"kubelet-runtime-boundary\", \"pluggable-interfaces\"]\n7\t---\n8\t# Container Runtime Interface (CRI) — kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/architecture/cri/\n9\t\n10\t> CHAPTER 2 §4 PRIMARY SOURCE. This page was not fetched by the book-outline\n11\t> stage; before it, the CRI rested on one clause in k8s-docs-containers.\n12\t\n13\t## The thesis sentence (use this one)\n14\t\n15\t\"The CRI is a plugin interface which enables the kubelet to use a wide variety of\n16\tcontainer runtimes, without having a need to recompile the cluster components.\"\n17\t\n18\t## Definition and requirement\n19\t\n20\t\"You need a working container runtime on each Node in your cluster, so that the\n21\tkubelet can launch Pods and their containers.\"\n22\t\n23\t\"The Container Runtime Interface (CRI) is the main protocol for the communication\n24\tbetween the kubelet and Container Runtime.\"\n25\t\n26\t\"The Kubernetes Container Runtime Interface (CRI) defines the main gRPC protocol\n27\tfor the communication between the node components kubelet and container runtime.\"\n28\t\n29\t## The API\n30\t\n31\tFEATURE STATE: Kubernetes v1.23 [stable]\n32\t\n33\t\"The kubelet acts as a client when connecting to the container runtime via gRPC.\n34\tThe runtime and image service endpoints have to be available in the container\n35\truntime, which can be configured separately within the kubelet by using the\n36\t`--container-runtime-endpoint` command line flag.\"\n37\t\n38\t\"For Kubernetes v1.26 and later, the kubelet requires that the container runtime\n39\tsupports the `v1` CRI API. If a container runtime does not support the `v1` API,\n40\tthe kubelet will not register the node.\"\n41\t\n42\t## Upgrading\n43\t\n44\t\"When upgrading the Kubernetes version on a node, the kubelet restarts. If the\n45\tcontainer runtime does not support the `v1` CRI API, the kubelet will fail to\n46\tregister and report an error.\"\n47\t\n48\t## List streaming\n49\t\n50\tFEATURE STATE: Kubernetes v1.36 [alpha] (disabled by default)\n51\t\n52\tThe standard CRI list RPCs (ListContainers, ListPodSandbox, ListImages) return all\n53\tresults in a single unary response; with the `CRIListStreaming` feature gate the\n54\tkubelet uses server-side streaming RPCs. \"If the container runtime does not support\n55\tstreaming RPCs, the kubelet automatically falls back to the standard unary RPCs for\n56\tbackward compatibility.\"\n57\t\n58\t## SCOPE WARNING FOR DRAFTING\n59\t\n60\tChapter 2 is a junior-tier associate chapter. Use ONLY the thesis sentence, the\n61\tdefinition, and \"the kubelet acts as a client\". The following are sourced here but\n62\tare NOT KCNA material and must not reach the draft:\n63\t  - --container-runtime-endpoint\n64\t  - the v1 CRI API requirement / version skew\n65\t  - gRPC message size limits\n66\t  - the CRIListStreaming feature gate\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"714f732e-6165-42bf-8392-8c603f3d60fe","uuid":"8b3dab3b-3535-4975-b053-063ab4a3a14c","timestamp":"2026-08-24T19:11:56.053Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\sources\\k8s-docs-cri-2026-08-24.md","content":"---\nsource_url: \"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/architecture/cri/\"\nfetched_at: \"2026-08-24T01:05:00-0400\"\nauthority: \"Kubernetes project (kubernetes.io/docs)\"\nobjectives_covered: [\"D1.4\"]\nconcepts_covered: [\"cri\", \"container-runtime\", \"kubelet-runtime-boundary\", \"pluggable-interfaces\"]\n---\n# Container Runtime Interface (CRI) — kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/architecture/cri/\n\n> CHAPTER 2 §4 PRIMARY SOURCE. This page was not fetched by the book-outline\n> stage; before it, the CRI rested on one clause in k8s-docs-containers.\n\n## The thesis sentence (use this one)\n\n\"The CRI is a plugin interface which enables the kubelet to use a wide variety of\ncontainer runtimes, without having a need to recompile the cluster components.\"\n\n## Definition and requirement\n\n\"You need a working container runtime on each Node in your cluster, so that the\nkubelet can launch Pods and their containers.\"\n\n\"The Container Runtime Interface (CRI) is the main protocol for the communication\nbetween the kubelet and Container Runtime.\"\n\n\"The Kubernetes Container Runtime Interface (CRI) defines the main gRPC protocol\nfor the communication between the node components kubelet and container runtime.\"\n\n## The API\n\nFEATURE STATE: Kubernetes v1.23 [stable]\n\n\"The kubelet acts as a client when connecting to the container runtime via gRPC.\nThe runtime and image service endpoints have to be available in the container\nruntime, which can be configured separately within the kubelet by using the\n`--container-runtime-endpoint` command line flag.\"\n\n\"For Kubernetes v1.26 and later, the kubelet requires that the container runtime\nsupports the `v1` CRI API. If a container runtime does not support the `v1` API,\nthe kubelet will not register the node.\"\n\n## Upgrading\n\n\"When upgrading the Kubernetes version on a node, the kubelet restarts. If the\ncontainer runtime does not support the `v1` CRI API, the kubelet will fail to\nregister and report an error.\"\n\n## List streaming\n\nFEATURE STATE: Kubernetes v1.36 [alpha] (disabled by default)\n\nThe standard CRI list RPCs (ListContainers, ListPodSandbox, ListImages) return all\nresults in a single unary response; with the `CRIListStreaming` feature gate the\nkubelet uses server-side streaming RPCs. \"If the container runtime does not support\nstreaming RPCs, the kubelet automatically falls back to the standard unary RPCs for\nbackward compatibility.\"\n\n## SCOPE WARNING FOR DRAFTING\n\nChapter 2 is a junior-tier associate chapter. Use ONLY the thesis sentence, the\ndefinition, and \"the kubelet acts as a client\". The following are sourced here but\nare NOT KCNA material and must not reach the draft:\n  - --container-runtime-endpoint\n  - the v1 CRI API requirement / version skew\n  - gRPC message size limits\n  - the CRIListStreaming feature gate\n","numLines":67,"startLine":1,"totalLines":67}}}
