{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Tcnfkj8CZfspokPn2WA2U5","type":"tool_result","content":"587\t## Tier 4 — Chapter 2 gap (shipped chapter, Stage 14 never ran)\n588\t\n589\t**No definitions written.** These are Chapter 2's to define, Chapter 2 shipped, and\n590\tChapter 2's Stage 14 did not run. Chapter 3 depends on every one.\n591\t\n592\t| Term | Defining chapter | Chapter 3's dependence |\n593\t|---|---|---|\n594\t| container image | Ch 2 §2 | Practice Q25 retrieval item |\n595\t| image layer / tag vs digest | Ch 2 §2–3 | Bearings #1 Q4 distractor D (\"cached container image layers\") |\n596\t| immutability (stateless & immutable) | Ch 2 §2 | Practice Q24 retrieval item; §6 \"replace, don't mutate\" |\n597\t| registry | Ch 2 §3 | Bearings #1 Q4 rationale |\n598\t| **CRI (Container Runtime Interface)** | Ch 2 §4 | Bearings #1 Q5 retrieval item; §3 census |\n599\t| containerd | Ch 2 §4 | §3 census; Practice Q13 |\n600\t| CRI-O | Ch 2 §4 | §3 census; Practice Q13 |\n601\t| runC | Ch 2 §4 | Ch 2's Fixed Point chain |\n602\t| RuntimeClass | Ch 2 §7 | not used in Ch 3 |\n603\t| relaxed isolation | Ch 2 §1 | §1 deployment eras; Practice Q2 |\n604\t| **\"Kubernetes defines an interface and lets the ecosystem implement it\"** | Ch 2 §4 (⚓, named) | ⚑ See Rule 6 flag below |\n605\t\n606\t> ⚑ **RULE 6 — Chapter 3 §3 broadens Chapter 2's named pattern past its enumeration.**\n607\t> Ch 3 §3 (draft line ~325) says of etcd and the container runtime: *\"That is the same\n608\t> architectural instinct… Where a good general-purpose component already exists,\n609\t> Kubernetes defines an interface and uses it rather than reimplementing it.\"*\n610\t>\n611\t> Chapter 2's pattern is specifically *\"Kubernetes defines an interface and lets the\n612\t> **ecosystem** implement it\"* (ch02:598), and its sourced enumeration is **CRI, CSI,\n613\t> CNI, device plugins, and API extensions**\n614\t> [source: k8s-docs-extending-kubernetes-2026-08-23]. **etcd is not among them** —\n615\t> Kubernetes does not define an etcd interface; it consumes a general-purpose datastore.\n616\t> The claim is true of the *runtime* and true-but-different of *etcd*, and calling them\n617\t> \"the same\" broadens a sourced list past what it says.\n618\t>\n619\t> Compounding it: ch02:596–598 is a section titled \"The pattern to name now\" whose ⚓\n620\t> tells the reader *\"Give this move a name in your head, because you are about to see it\n621\t> three more times.\"* Chapter 3 hits the first recurrence, re-derives it in fresh words,\n622\t> **and never uses the name or bears back to Ch 2 §4.** That is a missed spaced-retrieval\n623\t> event on a theme B3 tracks and Ch 17's secondary Zenith depends on.\n624\t>\n625\t> **Recommended chapter fix:** separate the two instincts — keep the named pattern for\n626\t> the container runtime, cross-beared to Ch 2 §4; describe etcd as the adjacent-but-\n627\t> distinct instinct of reusing an existing general-purpose component.\n628\t=== END WRITE ===\n629\t\n630\t=== WRITE C:\\dev\\lodestar\\certcomp\\..\\Book-KCNA/knowledge-base/concepts/control-loop.md ===\n631\t# Concept: The control loop"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"714f732e-6165-42bf-8392-8c603f3d60fe","uuid":"4c9fa2ea-814f-4fc9-a7a9-0300c30ff4d6","timestamp":"2026-08-24T19:12:47.318Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\.pipeline-state\\ch-03\\kb-manifest.md","content":"## Tier 4 — Chapter 2 gap (shipped chapter, Stage 14 never ran)\n\n**No definitions written.** These are Chapter 2's to define, Chapter 2 shipped, and\nChapter 2's Stage 14 did not run. Chapter 3 depends on every one.\n\n| Term | Defining chapter | Chapter 3's dependence |\n|---|---|---|\n| container image | Ch 2 §2 | Practice Q25 retrieval item |\n| image layer / tag vs digest | Ch 2 §2–3 | Bearings #1 Q4 distractor D (\"cached container image layers\") |\n| immutability (stateless & immutable) | Ch 2 §2 | Practice Q24 retrieval item; §6 \"replace, don't mutate\" |\n| registry | Ch 2 §3 | Bearings #1 Q4 rationale |\n| **CRI (Container Runtime Interface)** | Ch 2 §4 | Bearings #1 Q5 retrieval item; §3 census |\n| containerd | Ch 2 §4 | §3 census; Practice Q13 |\n| CRI-O | Ch 2 §4 | §3 census; Practice Q13 |\n| runC | Ch 2 §4 | Ch 2's Fixed Point chain |\n| RuntimeClass | Ch 2 §7 | not used in Ch 3 |\n| relaxed isolation | Ch 2 §1 | §1 deployment eras; Practice Q2 |\n| **\"Kubernetes defines an interface and lets the ecosystem implement it\"** | Ch 2 §4 (⚓, named) | ⚑ See Rule 6 flag below |\n\n> ⚑ **RULE 6 — Chapter 3 §3 broadens Chapter 2's named pattern past its enumeration.**\n> Ch 3 §3 (draft line ~325) says of etcd and the container runtime: *\"That is the same\n> architectural instinct… Where a good general-purpose component already exists,\n> Kubernetes defines an interface and uses it rather than reimplementing it.\"*\n>\n> Chapter 2's pattern is specifically *\"Kubernetes defines an interface and lets the\n> **ecosystem** implement it\"* (ch02:598), and its sourced enumeration is **CRI, CSI,\n> CNI, device plugins, and API extensions**\n> [source: k8s-docs-extending-kubernetes-2026-08-23]. **etcd is not among them** —\n> Kubernetes does not define an etcd interface; it consumes a general-purpose datastore.\n> The claim is true of the *runtime* and true-but-different of *etcd*, and calling them\n> \"the same\" broadens a sourced list past what it says.\n>\n> Compounding it: ch02:596–598 is a section titled \"The pattern to name now\" whose ⚓\n> tells the reader *\"Give this move a name in your head, because you are about to see it\n> three more times.\"* Chapter 3 hits the first recurrence, re-derives it in fresh words,\n> **and never uses the name or bears back to Ch 2 §4.** That is a missed spaced-retrieval\n> event on a theme B3 tracks and Ch 17's secondary Zenith depends on.\n>\n> **Recommended chapter fix:** separate the two instincts — keep the named pattern for\n> the container runtime, cross-beared to Ch 2 §4; describe etcd as the adjacent-but-\n> distinct instinct of reusing an existing general-purpose component.\n=== END WRITE ===\n\n=== WRITE C:\\dev\\lodestar\\certcomp\\..\\Book-KCNA/knowledge-base/concepts/control-loop.md ===\n# Concept: The control loop","numLines":45,"startLine":587,"totalLines":1696}}}
