{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VyXbWPF5yx7XKBvxbC11Th","type":"tool_result","content":"1931\t=== APPEND C:\\dev\\lodestar\\certcomp\\..\\Book-KCNA/knowledge-base/objective-coverage.md ===\n1932\t\n1933\t---\n1934\t\n1935\t## Chapter 7 update (2026-08-24)\n1936\t\n1937\t| Objective | First covered in | Depth | Last reviewed |\n1938\t|---|---|---|---|\n1939\t| **D1.3** | **Chapter 7** *(scheduling)* | **deep** | **2026-08-24** |\n1940\t\n1941\t**Registry row change:** `D1.3 | Scheduling | Ch 7` → status becomes **\"complete — Ch 7\n1942\tcovered 2026-08-24\"**, subject to the shortfall recorded below.\n1943\t\n1944\t**D1.3 opens and closes in one chapter.** Unlike D1.1 (four chapters, still in progress),\n1945\tthis objective has exactly one home. There is no later chapter to absorb a gap, which is why\n1946\tthe shortfall below is worth acting on rather than deferring.\n1947\t\n1948\t### Chapter 7 — D1.3 coverage detail\n1949\t\n1950\t`kb_tags.objectives: [\"D1.3\"]`; all seven sections carry `objectives: [\"D1.3\"]`.\n1951\t\n1952\t| Sub-topic | Depth |\n1953\t|---|---|\n1954\t| The two-step operation: filtering then scoring | **deep — discharges `control-plane-components.md`'s Ch 7 obligation** |\n1955\t| Binding as a notification; concretely, writing `.spec.nodeName` | **deep — closes Chapter 3's reserved term, with a physical referent** |\n1956\t| Feasible nodes; `PodFitsResources` | deep |\n1957\t| Random tie-break | deep — one sentence, correctly weighted |\n1958\t| Requests as filtering input; booked vs measured; Allocatable | **deep — discharges `resource-request.md`'s Ch 7 obligation, first of four** |\n1959\t| `Pending` as a state, not an error | **deep — Chapter 13's opening move depends on it** |\n1960\t| Node labels; the standard label set | moderate |\n1961\t| `nodeSelector` | deep |\n1962\t| Node affinity: six operators, two hardness levels, `IgnoredDuringExecution` | deep |\n1963\t| Taints: three effects and their timing | **deep — the chapter's densest recall block** |\n1964\t| Tolerations: matching, permits-never-attracts, dedicated-node pattern | **deep — the most durable error in this material** |\n1965\t| Built-in node-condition taints; the DaemonSet mechanism | moderate — **pays Chapter 6 §7's tease** ⚠ Ch 6 withdrawn |\n1966\t| Inter-Pod affinity / anti-affinity; `topologyKey` | moderate–deep |\n1967\t| Topology spread constraints: four fields | moderate — recognition depth, **outline OQ#2 closed** |\n1968\t| `nodeName`; the one failure that isn't `Pending` | deep |\n1969\t| `schedulerName` / custom scheduler | recognition — correctly scoped to Ch 17 |\n1970\t| Predicates / Priorities vocabulary map | moderate — ⚑ currency risk, recorded in the shard |\n1971\t| Priority / preemption / `PriorityClass` | named and scoped out — correct |\n1972\t| **Data locality · inter-workload interference · deadlines** | ⚑ **ABSENT — and Chapter 3 published them** |\n1973\t\n1974\t### ⚑ The one coverage shortfall — an integration debt, not a curriculum one\n1975\t\n1976\t`chapter-03:413` publishes the documentation's **six** scheduling factors verbatim:\n1977\t\"individual and collective resource requirements, hardware/software/policy constraints,\n1978\taffinity and anti-affinity specifications, **data locality**, **inter-workload interference**,\n1979\tand **deadlines**.\"\n1980\t\n1981\tChapter 7 owes the detail and delivers three of six, never mentioning the other three — not\n1982\teven to scope them out. Curriculum-alignment logged this as **D1.3-09 PARTIAL**.\n1983\t\n1984\tThe knowledge-base cost is distinct from the coverage cost: a reader who remembers Chapter 3's\n1985\tlist gets no acknowledgement that half of it was dropped. That is the order/truth-balance\n1986\tfailure skill Part 11 warns about, and **Chapter 7 already models the correct fix twice** —\n1987\tthe preemption clause (\"Register that they exist so that nothing in this chapter reads as a\n1988\tlie later\") and the `minDomains` mention. One sentence in §2 or §7 closes it.\n1989\t\n1990\t---\n1991\t\n1992\t## ⚑ Book-level: the domain-allocation alarm has eased\n1993\t\n1994\tChapter 5's ledger raised this as blocking before Chapter 6 drafts. Chapter 7's number changes\n1995\tthe arithmetic.\n1996\t\n1997\t| Chapter | Claimed | Objective | Metadata form |\n1998\t|---|---|---|---|\n1999\t| Ch 2 — Containerization | ~9% | D1.1 | discloses \"authored allocation\" inline, source-tagged |\n2000\t| Ch 3 — Cluster architecture | ~6% | D1.1 | \"authored estimate\" |\n2001\t| Ch 4 — Objects | ~6% | D1.1 | no caveat |\n2002\t| Ch 5 — Pods | 7% | D1.1 | \"This book's allocation\" — no caveat, no tag |\n2003\t| **Ch 7 — Scheduling** | **5%** | **D1.3** | separate italic disclosure line — **clearest content, least conformant form** |\n2004\t| **Subtotal** | **33% of 44%** | | |\n2005\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"714f732e-6165-42bf-8392-8c603f3d60fe","uuid":"50783de4-ced2-44ae-90ff-f463a103fb85","timestamp":"2026-08-24T19:12:52.793Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\.pipeline-state\\ch-07\\kb-manifest.md","content":"=== APPEND C:\\dev\\lodestar\\certcomp\\..\\Book-KCNA/knowledge-base/objective-coverage.md ===\n\n---\n\n## Chapter 7 update (2026-08-24)\n\n| Objective | First covered in | Depth | Last reviewed |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **D1.3** | **Chapter 7** *(scheduling)* | **deep** | **2026-08-24** |\n\n**Registry row change:** `D1.3 | Scheduling | Ch 7` → status becomes **\"complete — Ch 7\ncovered 2026-08-24\"**, subject to the shortfall recorded below.\n\n**D1.3 opens and closes in one chapter.** Unlike D1.1 (four chapters, still in progress),\nthis objective has exactly one home. There is no later chapter to absorb a gap, which is why\nthe shortfall below is worth acting on rather than deferring.\n\n### Chapter 7 — D1.3 coverage detail\n\n`kb_tags.objectives: [\"D1.3\"]`; all seven sections carry `objectives: [\"D1.3\"]`.\n\n| Sub-topic | Depth |\n|---|---|\n| The two-step operation: filtering then scoring | **deep — discharges `control-plane-components.md`'s Ch 7 obligation** |\n| Binding as a notification; concretely, writing `.spec.nodeName` | **deep — closes Chapter 3's reserved term, with a physical referent** |\n| Feasible nodes; `PodFitsResources` | deep |\n| Random tie-break | deep — one sentence, correctly weighted |\n| Requests as filtering input; booked vs measured; Allocatable | **deep — discharges `resource-request.md`'s Ch 7 obligation, first of four** |\n| `Pending` as a state, not an error | **deep — Chapter 13's opening move depends on it** |\n| Node labels; the standard label set | moderate |\n| `nodeSelector` | deep |\n| Node affinity: six operators, two hardness levels, `IgnoredDuringExecution` | deep |\n| Taints: three effects and their timing | **deep — the chapter's densest recall block** |\n| Tolerations: matching, permits-never-attracts, dedicated-node pattern | **deep — the most durable error in this material** |\n| Built-in node-condition taints; the DaemonSet mechanism | moderate — **pays Chapter 6 §7's tease** ⚠ Ch 6 withdrawn |\n| Inter-Pod affinity / anti-affinity; `topologyKey` | moderate–deep |\n| Topology spread constraints: four fields | moderate — recognition depth, **outline OQ#2 closed** |\n| `nodeName`; the one failure that isn't `Pending` | deep |\n| `schedulerName` / custom scheduler | recognition — correctly scoped to Ch 17 |\n| Predicates / Priorities vocabulary map | moderate — ⚑ currency risk, recorded in the shard |\n| Priority / preemption / `PriorityClass` | named and scoped out — correct |\n| **Data locality · inter-workload interference · deadlines** | ⚑ **ABSENT — and Chapter 3 published them** |\n\n### ⚑ The one coverage shortfall — an integration debt, not a curriculum one\n\n`chapter-03:413` publishes the documentation's **six** scheduling factors verbatim:\n\"individual and collective resource requirements, hardware/software/policy constraints,\naffinity and anti-affinity specifications, **data locality**, **inter-workload interference**,\nand **deadlines**.\"\n\nChapter 7 owes the detail and delivers three of six, never mentioning the other three — not\neven to scope them out. Curriculum-alignment logged this as **D1.3-09 PARTIAL**.\n\nThe knowledge-base cost is distinct from the coverage cost: a reader who remembers Chapter 3's\nlist gets no acknowledgement that half of it was dropped. That is the order/truth-balance\nfailure skill Part 11 warns about, and **Chapter 7 already models the correct fix twice** —\nthe preemption clause (\"Register that they exist so that nothing in this chapter reads as a\nlie later\") and the `minDomains` mention. One sentence in §2 or §7 closes it.\n\n---\n\n## ⚑ Book-level: the domain-allocation alarm has eased\n\nChapter 5's ledger raised this as blocking before Chapter 6 drafts. Chapter 7's number changes\nthe arithmetic.\n\n| Chapter | Claimed | Objective | Metadata form |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Ch 2 — Containerization | ~9% | D1.1 | discloses \"authored allocation\" inline, source-tagged |\n| Ch 3 — Cluster architecture | ~6% | D1.1 | \"authored estimate\" |\n| Ch 4 — Objects | ~6% | D1.1 | no caveat |\n| Ch 5 — Pods | 7% | D1.1 | \"This book's allocation\" — no caveat, no tag |\n| **Ch 7 — Scheduling** | **5%** | **D1.3** | separate italic disclosure line — **clearest content, least conformant form** |\n| **Subtotal** | **33% of 44%** | | |\n","numLines":75,"startLine":1931,"totalLines":2211}}}
